Negotiations in Singapore
On June 12 in Singapore held the first in the history of negotiations between the leaders of the United States and North Korea.
After a serious aggravation of relations and Mutual Threats to the Use of Nuclear Weapons, the summit looked a turning point in the protracted American-Korean crisis.
At the end of the negotiations, the parties expressed their intention to move towards a peaceful resolution of contradictions, although they did not take on any legal obligations.
Possitative results of the meeting were the cessation of nuclear and missile tests of the DPRK, as well as the return to the United States, the remains of U.S American soldiers.
At the same time, other practical steps towards the denuclearization of North Korea are still stunned.
Media reported that after the Singapore summit, the United States has already sent the DPRK several scenarios for dismantling, but Pyongyang rejected them, calling them “Gangster”.
