Violations recorded in the referendum in Macedonia
Four incidents related to violations of the electoral legislation are registered in the Republic of Macedonia in a referendum on an intergovernmental agreement with Greece on renaissance.
This was announced on Sunday by the press Secretary of the Ministry of internal Affairs Tony Angelovsky.
Since the opening of the polling stations, 4 incidents have been recorded that have been eliminated,” he said.
At the polling station in elementary school "Lazo Angelovsky" in Skopje, a 22-year-old K.Zh. violated public order and tranquillity, insulted the citizens and attacked the police.
He was apprehended and taken to a police station.
According to the representative of the foreign Ministry, all the violators were immediately taken to police stations.
The Ministry noted that in relation to all violations is being checked.
“Ministries will act in accordance with the law so that citizens can quietly use the constitutional right to freely express their will.
We urge citizens to comply with the laws and to refrain from any violations of public order and tranquility and any violation of the secrecy of the vote”, – said the representative of the Ministry of internal Affairs.
Citizens during the referendum on Sunday are invited to answer one question: “Do you support EU-NATO membership by accepting an agreement between the Republic of Madepoynia and the Greek Republic?”
Referendum is designed to resolve a 27-year-old spore between the Macedonia and Greece regarding the name of the former Yugoslav republic, which coincides with the denoy of the northern Greek region.
The foreign Ministers of Macedonia and Greece on June 17 during a solemn ceremonial ceremony on the shore of Lake Prespa, on which the border between the two countries takes place, signed an agreement on a new official naming of the former Yugoslav Republic.
It provides for the use of the name "Re-Republic of North Macedonia".
This agreement should decide not only a long-term dispute about the name of the country, but also to open Skopje the way to NATO and the European Union.
The Minister of foreign Affairs of Syria: Russia’s decision on the delivery of the S-300 is a timely step
The decision of Russia to supply anti-aircraft missile systems (SAMs) of the S-300 to Syria is a timely step.
