Pashinyan hopes to hold early elections to the Armenian parliament in 2018
The elections to the Armenian Parliament can be held in 2018, said Prime Minister Nikol Pashinyan.
“It is not excluded, until the end of the year”, the head of the government replied to the question of journalists about the timing of their holding (quoted by “Interfax”).
President Pashinyan also did not rule out that he would “bring people to the streets again” to hold early elections, if the discussion of this issue with parliamentary forces is not crowned by a success.
But I am determined to hold negotiations with parliamentary forces.
I hope that they are also inclined to a constructive dialogue”, – quotes the Prime Minister “Novosti-Armenia”.
Nikol Pashinyan adds that the early elections are a “requirement of the people”, as well as a part of the program of the government, for which the parliament voted.
“The long-term vision of the government”, according to him, it is also necessary to attract investments and develop the economy.
At the UN General General Assembly in New York, Mr. Pashinyan promised after returning to Yerevan to begin “negotiations with representatives of all parliamentary as well as extra-Parliamentary forces in order to discuss the time and conditions of early elections”.
In the current parliament, about half of the deputies represent the Republican Party of Armenia, which is opposed to Mr. Pashinyan.
Early voting is impossible without the dissolution of the parliament, and there are no legal grounds for this yet.
