Accusation for the Dagestani deputy became the news
The Soviet district court of Makhachkala detained for two months the Deputy of the people’s Assembly of Dagestan Rajab Abdulatipov, suspected of participating in a criminal community who issued a disability for bribes.
“Kommersant” became a well-receipidim of the details of the materials of the investigation, shelting light on how, according to the Investigative Committee of Russia, the junior brother of the former head of the Republic Ramazan Abdultipov Rajab Abdulatipov contributed to the criminal acts of the now former head of the Main Bureau of medical and social expertise, Magomed Makhachiv and his accomplices.
Among other things, during the operational-search activities carried out by employees of the interior Ministry, it was established that Rajab Abdulatipov lobbied the appointment of Magomed Makhachev to the position of the head of the bureau, allegedly having received 70 million rubles for this.
We will remind, earlier the investigation against Magomed Makhachev, other managers and employees of the Territorial Bureau of Physic and Social Examination, who are under its subordination, initiated a criminal case under Article 210 (creating a criminal community using an official situation and participating in it), Art. 290 (receiving a bribe by an organized group), Art. 292 (official forgery) and article 159
As follows from the materials of the investigation, at the end of 2013 Razhab Abdulatipov, aware of the illegal actions of Magomed Makhachev and his accustomers engaged in embezzling funds of the Retivenation Fund, joined their activities, entering into a criminal community.
While serving as the head of the department of the Federal Migration Service of Russia for Dagestan and having links in state authorities and law enforcement agencies, as well as taking advantage of his kinship relations with the head of Dagestan, Rajab Abdulatipov, according to investigators, "providing the activities of other members of the criminal community, established contacts with government officials to support the illegal activities of Magomed Makhachev and his being in the position of the head of the federal).
After the announcement of this information at the meeting of the Soviet district court on Friday, Rajab Abdulatipov rejected the accusations presented to him.
“Of course, everything that is presented to me today as an accusation, for me everything is new, I completely don’t familiar with it,” he said.
