Named the period of death of the universe
The universe will last another 140 billion years, which is ten times the age of observable world, amounting about 13.8 billion years.
The study of an international group of scientists is published in the library of electronic preprits arXiv.org and is aimed at publication in the journal Publications of the Astronomical Society of Japan, according to the Japanese newspaper Asahi Shimbun.
To such inferences, experts came, obscurant with HSC (Hyper Suprime-Cam) the Subaru Telescope for about ten millions of galley galaxies.
Tracking the distribution of dark matter and dark energy, which accounted for more than 95 per cent of observable world energy, scientists, working as part of a standard ΛCDM (Λ Cold Dark Matter), assessed the rate of enlargement of the universe, which turned out to be slightly slower than previously thought.
In the press-relative of the Subaru observatory it is noted that the observations made it possible to obtain a detailed three-dimensional map of the distribution of matter in the universe, and the data of the European Space Telescope Planck clarified the restrictions imposed on the parameters of ΛCDM.
In July, scientists simulated the possible death of the universe.
Three years earlier, their co-colleagues presented new arguments in favor that the observed world will cease to exist after 22 billion years as a result of the Great Bang.
Failed another attempt to unify the initiators of the pension referendum
Opportunity to know the opinion of the people about the pension reform is postponed for an indebted period
In Moscow on Saturday there was a meeting of the all-federal initiative group of the referendum against raising the retirement age.
It was attended by representatives of 13 sub-guided subgroups who registered different wording of the issues (the Central Election Commission only registered five formulations).
They decided to apply to the CEC with a request to register a single initiative group and ask the Russians a question: "Are you to ensure that the established legislation on pensions as of July 1, 2018, the age at which Russian citizens get the right to an old-growfity pension is not increased?"
This wording was registered by the Vologda subgroup, whose representatives did not participate in the meeting, but it was considered the simplest and most legally capacious.
Most of the participants of the congregation consisted of supporters of a member of “Just-Suspied Russia” Ilya Sviridov (six subgroups) and the CPRF (four subgroups).
They were united by three independent subgroups - from Nizhny Novgorod, Voronezh and Orenburg.
Sviridov previously told Vedomosti that invitations were sent to all initiators, and representatives of about 40 subgroups expressed their consent to come.
But, for example, Marina Semenova, who headed the Vologda subgroup (its wording was supported by another 15 subgroups), told Vedomosti that she did not receive an invitation and did not plan to come: “We didn’t figure out who’s a friend and who the enemy is.”
