Supersonic passenger aircraft in the Russian Federation will be put for serial production
Serial production of supersonic passenger aircraft in Russia will begin after 2030.
This was stated by the General Director of the Central aerohydromygine Institute of Zhukovsky Kirill Sypalot.
According to him, the scientific center conducts work on supersonic topics both in the framework of international consortia and cooperation with the Ministry of Industry and Trade.
“According to our feelings, it will take us two or three years to get a technology demonstrating demonstrator, as well as another 10-15 years to receive a serial machine that allows you to carry out transportation through the expanses of our homeland,” Sypalo added.
He said that now before Russian specialists there is a question of how to make the technique of economical and safe at the same time.
In the beginning of September, the developer of aviation equipment PJSC “Tupolev” announced the completion of pre-design work on a supersonic passenger aircraft, according to calculations, the aircraft will be able to reach a speed of up to 1900 km / h at an altitude of 11 km.
This was announced by the Deputy General Director of the enterprise Valery Solzobov.
The President of Ukraine Petro Poroshenko thanked Russian President Volodymyr Vladimir Putin for the fact that he made Ukraine more European.
