The foreign Minister of Germany honored the memory of the victims of Nazism
An action was held in Marzabetto in the north of Italy to commemorate the victims of punitive operation of the Nazis, during which about 770 people were killed in September-October 1944.
The majority of them are women and children.
German Foreign Minister Heiko Maas participated in the ceremonies this year.
He said that "with deep sorrow and great disgrace" leaned towards the victims of the murder and their families.
Ma'as promised to oppose nationalism the struggle for freedom, mutual respect and the friendship between Italy and Germany.
Together with the German minister in Marzabetto came his Italian colleague Enzo Maawvero-Milanesi.
The Italian Foreign Ministry emphasizes that the foreign ministers for the first time together participate in the ceremonies and this symbolizes the aspirations of both countries to preserve the memory of the crimes of the past.
