Peenager “Syrius” discussed with the scientists the nature-like technologies
Pupils of the Syrius educational center in Sochi, participants of the School of Agrobiology and Plant Genetics, visited a lecture by scientists of the national research center "Kurchatov Institute".
Speech of the researchers took place within the framework of the Global international forum of converged and nature-like technologies, organized in Sochi on the instructions of Russian President Vladimir Putin, according to the website of the educational center on September 29.
The Lecture was opened by a documentary "Code of Kurchatov", during which the President of the Kurchatov Institute, Corresponding Member of the Russian Academy of Sciences Mikhail Kovalchuk spoke about the global challenges as the driving force for the development of civilization.
Lecture of the Scientist is published on the "Syrius website".
Schoolchildren have learned that modern technologies need a huge amount of energy.
Alternate energy is not yet able to produce such volumes.
To solve this problem, according to the organizers of the forum, will help the nature-similar technologies that young scientists are currently working on.
In addition, Kovalchuk raised the topic of responsibility for the development of nature-like technologies, and also spoke about the risks, which inevitably occurs when creating such technologies.
"The coming of such technologies is a unique thing, it is a colossal good.
This is an explosive increase in medical technologies, it is an improvement in the quality of life and infrastructure.
But there is a second side as well.
