Vucic left in force the highest level of combat-readiness of the Serbian army
Serbian President Aleksandr Vucic ordered to put in force the highest level of combat preparedness, to which the armed forces of the country were given due to the situation in the north of the autonomous province of Kosovo and Metohija.
“The President has ordered to maintain the highest level of combat preparedness, its cancellation there will be a separate order,” Serbian Defense Minister Oleksandr Vulin said on Sunday.
According to him, the head of state is deeply concerned about the events in Kosov.
At the same time, Vulin boasted, the President of the Republic expressed “pleasure with energy, the work, readiness and the velocity of the military of Serbia”.
Vucic himself said on the eve that the situation in Kosovo and Metohija he intends to discuss with the President of Russia Vladimir Putin and to ask the Russian leader for support.
According to reports, the meeting is scheduled for October 2 and should take place in Moscow.
Simultaneously, the Serbian leader stressed that he will do everything to preserve peace, and noted that he would like his country to be a peaceful, successful country of the future.
Last Saturday, September 29, despite the ban provided for by international treaties, several dozen of the Kosovo special forces moved to the territory inhabited by Serbs of northern Kosov and Metohija, taking positions around the Gazivode reservoir, taking control of Ghazivode hydroelectric power plants and invading the Environmental and Development Center in the village of Zubin-Pot.
This was done in connection in connection with the visit to the north of the region of President Hashima Thaci.
After for some time, the Kosovo special forces left the occupied positions.
It was after this that the President of Serbia led the armed forces of the country and the special forces of the police into full combat readiness, and also expressed protest to NATO Secretary General Jens Stoltenberg.
