Defending Ukrainian citizens, I defend the sovereignty of our state.
In the same way, as we respect the sovereignty of other states, we demand the same respect for Ukraine”, – said Poroshenko.
According to Poroshenko, as a president he will protect Ukrainian citizens, no matter where they are - in the east or in the west of the country.
Simultaneously, the head of state supported the position of the foreign Ministry in the passport scandal with Hungary, which consists in the intention to expel the consul of this country from Beregovo.
“I completely share every letter that the foreign Ministry said”, – said the President.
As reported by “FACTS”, on September 19 in the network there was a video, which recorded the date of issuance to the citizens of Ukraine at the consulate of Hungary in Beregovo Hungarian passports was recorded.
At the same time, they took an oath of allegiance of Hungary aloud.
The Minister of foreign Affairs of Ukraine Pavel Klymkin noted that the consul of Hungary, who appears on the video with the distribution of Hungarian passports to Ukrainians, must leave the territory of Ukraine either by the decision of Budapest himself or will be deported by Kiev.
It also became known that the Prosecutor’s office of the Transcarpathian region opened a criminal case on the fact of the issuance of Hungarian passports.
