More than 10 million Syrians have become refugees since the beginning of the armed conflict, which has been going on in Syria for a period of seven years.
Approximately five million people have escaped to other countries, first of all, to neighboring Turkey, Lebanon and Jordan.
Now, according to Damascus, military actions are close to an end, and the country is ready to voluntarily return refugees.
This was stated by the Minister of foreign Affairs of Syria Walid al-Muallem, speaking at the United Nations: “Current time the situation on the ground has become more stable and secure thanks to the successes achieved in the fight against terrorism.
The government continues its restoration work in areas destroyed by terrorists, returning them to a normal life.
All conditions have been created for the voluntary return of Syrian refugees to a country they had to leave because of terrified terrorism and unilateral economic sanctions that complicated people’s lives and deprived them of their means of subsistence.
The Syrian authorities also called upon the international community to facilitate the return of the refugees and to allocate funds for this.
In the meantime, the U.S. and EU countries are refusing to provide Syria with assistance, stating that a political solution to the conflict must first be found.
“Volkswagen” has fully pleaded guilty to “dyselgeate” in January 2017.
In December last year, Oliver Schmidt was sentenced to seven years in prison - one of the managers of an American branch of the company.
The group's losses are valued by at least 25 billion euros.
This amount includes not only fines and compensation.
Until June next year, the automaker is obliged to repurchase or correct 85% of the cars involved in the scandal.
In February, the management of the company said that the obligations have already been fulfilled in relation to 83% of the cars, so that the program will be completed ahead of schedule.
“Volkswagen” is trying to compensate for the losses and restore the trust of customers.
So, recently the management of the concern has again changed again, and large-scale restructuring and fundamental changes in the management system have also been announced.
Moreover, “Volkswagen” promises to redeem even new cars, if the German cities are banned by diesel trees on their streets: this right of the authorities received in February of this year.
Approximatory typhoon paralyzed transport communication in Japan
The largest railway operator in the Japan railway operator Japan Railways announced the suspension of high-explosive trains due to the impending typhoon "Trami".
Restriction from 17:00 (from 11:00 to Moscow time) will be extended to routes between the central region with the western and south-western parts of the country.
Because of the impending scrueties, the movement of regular buses running between the large cities of these regions and Tokyo will also be suspended.
Local television told about the abolition of more than 1126 flights at airports in Japan, the agency “RIA Novosti” clarifies on September 30.
The authorities of the country said about the suspension of the ferry service.
According to the main meteorological agency of the country, now "Trami" is located 90 km from the city of Miyazaki, on the island of Kyushu.
He's assigned serial number 24.
The wind speed in the center of the typhoon is 45 m / s, with gusts of the wind - up to 60 m / s.
Meteorologists qualifies it as “extremely strong”.
They are also warning of a powerful stormy wind, which accompanies a Tropical Cyclone.
In July, the authorities of Japan calculated the damage from torrential rains, which led to floods and landslides in the west of the country.
It amounted to about ¥44 billion (approximately $400 million).
The number of victims at that time exceeded 200 people, dozens were missing.
