Every inhabitant of Kalmyk is indebted
Residents of the republic are increasingly visiting the official website of the Office of the Federal Bailiff Service of Russia for the Republic of Kazakhstan.
According to the specialists of the department of organizational and control work, informatization and information security of the republican agency, over the past eight months, more than 140 thousand visits to the site itself have been registered, more than 42 thousand are more than 42 thousand - the section "Bank of these enforcement productions", 661 payment receipts for payment of debts have been downloaded.
Valery Bogdanov, Chairman of the Public Council under the UFSSP of Russia for the Republic of Kazakhstan Valery Bogdanov, for almost every resident of the region there are debts for utilities, traffic police fines, bank loans, loans, and no one is insured against unforeseen situations.
Debtors can await the negative consequences in the form, for example, the prohibition of traveling abroad.
That's why UFSSP of Russia in the Republic of Kazakhstan recommends to everyone who has planned a trip abroad to clarify in the bailiff's bailiff department at the place of residency or on the website www.r08fssprus.ru information about the availability of unpaid debts and repay them.
The service has created the "Ts of data of enforcement proceedings" for the convenience of citizens.
This special electronic application is located not only on the regional UFSSP sites of Russia, but also in social networks and means of mobile communication iPad, iPhone and a smartphone.
In the data bank contains information about the enforcement proceedings initiated by Kalmyk bailiffs in relation to all deblers, - explains the assistant to the head of the UFSSP of Russia for the Republic of Kazakhstan Delgir Bodgaeva.
“In the presence of arrears, the system withdraplifies information about the number and the date of initiation of the enforcement proceeding; the name of the body that issued the wrise or an other act; its number, the amount and type of debt; address of the bailiff’s bailiff’s department; the bailiff’s bailiff’s name; a contact phone.
Information about the course of enforcement proceedings can also be obtained on the portal of public services at http://epgu.gosuslugi.
