The EU has allocated €1.5 million to help the victims in Indonesia
The European Union (EU) has allocated €1.5 million to Indonesia to combat the effects of the earthquake and tsunami.
On September 30, the press service of the European Commission reported on September 30.
In order to overwhelm the European Commission dispatched its experts.
As it is noted, the funds will go to disinfection, as well as to provide victims with food, water, temporary shelters and medicines.
