The Ministry of Finance of the Russian Federation predicted the ruble for 17 years ahead
The Ministry of Finance of Russia expects a gradual easing of the ruble - up to 73.9 rubles per dollar by 2031-2035, it follows from the long-term budget forecast submitted to the state Duma together with the draft federal budget.
In 2021-20-25 the ruble, according to the forecast, will be 66.4 ruble per dollar, in 2026-2030 - 71.1 roubles, and in the next five years - 73.9.
The department notes that these figures are a nominal rate.
The real effective rate (indicator, taking into account the changes in the exchange rates of countries that are the main trading partners of the Russian Federation) will remain stable, officials assure.
As for inflorescance, until 2020 it will be 3.5%, and then stabilize at about 4%, according to the Ministry of Finance.
