Peskov answered the question about the possible support of Serbia in Kosovo
The press Secretary of the President of Russia Dmitry Peskov believes that it is too early to talk about whether Russia will provide assistance to Serbia after an aggravation in Kosovo.
Negotiations between the leaders of the two countries should first take place.
The representative of the Kremlin told the journalists of the radio station “Moscow speaking” on Sunday, September 30.
On September 29, a citizen of Serbia Aleksandr Vucic said that he intends to discuss the situation in Kosovo with Russian President Volodymyr Putin at the next meeting in Moscow on October 2.
The Serbian leader also planned to ask the support of Moscow in the current situation, specifying that there is no talk of military assistance in this case.
Vucic noted that he would like to preserve peace in the region and intends to do everything necessary for this.
Earlier in the same day it became known that the President of Serbia ordered to bring the armed forces of the country into a state of higher combat readiness.
